1
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:35,009
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:37,729
[Episode 18]

3
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,560
Gosh, I just realized.

4
00:01:41,430 --> 00:01:43,289
You're celebrating, aren't you?

5
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:44,509
Or are you discussing

6
00:01:44,509 --> 00:01:45,789
what to do next?

7
00:01:46,789 --> 00:01:48,120
If I'm not mistaken,

8
00:01:48,789 --> 00:01:50,720
Song Xiaoguang should be released

9
00:01:50,950 --> 00:01:53,080
on medical parole in a few days, right?

10
00:02:11,360 --> 00:02:13,360
The Song family paid me 50,000 yuan.

11
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:16,960
About this thick, a stack.

12
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,980
In exchange for my daughter's...

13
00:02:21,910 --> 00:02:23,079
life,

14
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:24,710
cut short at 25.

15
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,600
I accepted the money.

16
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:30,890
I had to.

17
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,400
I still have to live

18
00:02:33,710 --> 00:02:35,310
and do business in Binjiang.

19
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:39,010
But I want to ask you something—

20
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:41,750
after what you did,

21
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:43,710
deep down,

22
00:02:44,079 --> 00:02:45,140
can you really live

23
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:47,079
with yourselves?

24
00:02:59,590 --> 00:03:00,360
Mr. Qiao,

25
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,800
I did everything I could.

26
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,890
My conscience is clear.

27
00:03:08,400 --> 00:03:09,870
Your conscience is clear?

28
00:03:11,710 --> 00:03:13,310
Those two flatbread sellers

29
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,400
stripped a woman

30
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,730
of her clothes in a fight

31
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,400
and got suspended death sentences.

32
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,310
A high-ranking official's son

33
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:21,770
who violated so many women

34
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:23,190
only got 5 years.

35
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:24,870
Why?

36
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:26,790
Can any of you tell me

37
00:03:26,810 --> 00:03:27,970
why?

38
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:29,630
Is it because they didn't have

39
00:03:29,630 --> 00:03:32,190
50,000 yuan to compensate
the victim's family?

40
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:34,120
Or because you're all afraid of
the powerful

41
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:35,710
and only dare to bully ordinary people—

42
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:38,310
treating people differently
based on their status?

43
00:03:38,310 --> 00:03:39,000
Mr. Qiao,

44
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:41,520
you can't just say things like that.

45
00:03:41,870 --> 00:03:42,590
The law

46
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:44,150
has its principles.

47
00:03:44,450 --> 00:03:45,800
The court has its own judgments.

48
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:46,829
It's not like you can do

49
00:03:46,829 --> 00:03:47,540
whatever you want.

50
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:48,690
So I'm someone who does

51
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:49,680
whatever he wants?

52
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,840
I want Song Xiaoguang sentenced to life!

53
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,120
I want him sentenced to death!

54
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:54,079
Can I do that?

55
00:03:58,530 --> 00:03:59,910
Your comrade here said that well.

56
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:01,170
Very well said indeed!

57
00:04:01,590 --> 00:04:03,250
"Principles," "judgments."

58
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:04,770
Then let me ask you:

59
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,870
what are your principles?

60
00:04:07,750 --> 00:04:09,480
How do you make your judgments?

61
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:13,030
Do you use the law in your hands

62
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,960
to judge who is easy to mess with

63
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:16,019
and who is not, huh?

64
00:04:16,029 --> 00:04:16,860
Are you done?

65
00:04:20,070 --> 00:04:21,130
Isn't that enough?

66
00:04:22,910 --> 00:04:24,190
He's been holding back this whole time.

67
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:25,480
Don't push your luck!

68
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:27,830
Yu Gaoyuan and I were classmates
for many years.

69
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:29,160
I'm also his colleague.

70
00:04:29,270 --> 00:04:31,000
I know what kind of person he is.

71
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:31,600
And I know

72
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:33,000
what he did

73
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:34,830
for this case.

74
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,850
He's had his own struggles.

75
00:04:37,070 --> 00:04:39,000
He really did everything he could.

76
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:40,430
He's lived up to

77
00:04:40,430 --> 00:04:41,600
his role as a judge

78
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:42,360
and upheld his integrity

79
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:43,760
as a legal professional!

80
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:51,220
We're all deeply saddened...

81
00:04:53,430 --> 00:04:55,360
by what happened to your daughter.

82
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:58,380
I understand how you feel.

83
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:01,750
But that doesn't give you the right

84
00:05:01,750 --> 00:05:02,870
to maliciously speculate about him

85
00:05:02,870 --> 00:05:04,930
or humiliate him however you please!

86
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:11,750
To your daughter.

87
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:17,480
Don't...

88
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:24,480
Stop drinking.

89
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,080
Enough! N-No more drinking!

90
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,720
Let this matter go.

91
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:44,690
Let's all move forward,

92
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:46,390
okay?

93
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,409
You guys go on celebrating.

94
00:06:13,230 --> 00:06:19,990
♪ The first light of dawn
spills across the table ♪

95
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:26,140
♪ Every stroke defines the line
between good and evil ♪

96
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,890
♪ Behind every verdict ♪

97
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:34,740
♪ Lie words left unspoken ♪

98
00:06:33,480 --> 00:06:33,920
Tian.

99
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:42,990
♪ And souls left broken ♪

100
00:06:38,750 --> 00:06:39,120
Tian.

101
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:40,560
This pack's not bad.

102
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,330
Have one.

103
00:06:41,950 --> 00:06:43,010
Let's go, let's go.

104
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:44,630
♪ No need to ask him ♪

105
00:06:44,659 --> 00:06:49,440
♪ How reason and passion make peace ♪

106
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,680
Don't talk to anyone in this family.

107
00:06:51,220 --> 00:06:52,260
♪ Just watch him ♪

108
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:57,620
♪ A light in hand,
keeping vigil at the edge of the abyss ♪

109
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,370
♪ On the scales ♪

110
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:05,790
♪ Suffering weighs against our vows ♪

111
00:07:05,810 --> 00:07:07,240
♪ Who doesn't ♪

112
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:13,370
♪ Weigh principle against compromise
within their conscience? ♪

113
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:15,330
Come on.

114
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,070
Thank you. Thank you very much.

115
00:07:18,070 --> 00:07:19,510
-Pleasure doing business with you.
-Likewise.

116
00:07:19,510 --> 00:07:20,040
Win-win.

117
00:07:20,750 --> 00:07:21,280
This way.

118
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:22,830
See you next time.

119
00:07:23,950 --> 00:07:24,360
Bye.

120
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:24,920
Bye.

121
00:07:28,870 --> 00:07:29,600
Done.

122
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:30,190
♪ We don't care ♪

123
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:30,510
It's done.

124
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:35,370
♪ If we become a footnote in the case ♪

125
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:31,950
We've got the deal!

126
00:07:34,310 --> 00:07:35,000
Come on, you two.

127
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,120
Stand a little closer together.

128
00:07:36,120 --> 00:07:37,159
That's right, closer.

129
00:07:36,650 --> 00:07:37,570
♪ Because ♪

130
00:07:37,590 --> 00:07:42,970
♪ Even ordinary souls
can make truth their crown ♪

131
00:07:37,750 --> 00:07:38,880
Alright, get ready.

132
00:07:41,270 --> 00:07:42,430
Now, smile.

133
00:07:43,070 --> 00:07:45,790
One, two, three.

134
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:45,880
♪ As the tides rise and fall ♪

135
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:51,190
♪ Dust stands beside eternity ♪

136
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,430
♪ We all long to see ♪

137
00:07:52,220 --> 00:07:55,680
[Binjiang Party Secretary Song Encheng Under Investigation
for Alleged Disciplinary Violations]

138
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:54,400
♪ As the years go by ♪

139
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:58,100
♪ That face from our younger days ♪

140
00:07:58,490 --> 00:07:59,620
♪ We will all ♪

141
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:01,330
♪ Behold the face of justice ♪

142
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:06,490
♪ In the end ♪

143
00:08:21,360 --> 00:08:23,620
Who were you on the phone with
for so long?

144
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,190
One of Dad's former comrades

145
00:08:30,190 --> 00:08:32,030
who works at the Ministry of Justice now.

146
00:08:32,030 --> 00:08:33,270
I just called him

147
00:08:33,270 --> 00:08:34,470
and talked about you.

148
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:36,890
What did he say?

149
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,299
He said the Supreme People's Court

150
00:08:39,299 --> 00:08:41,159
is indeed very interested in you.

151
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,120
But because of the Song Xiaoguang case,

152
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,840
that guy Qiao has been filing complaints
about you everywhere,

153
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:47,000
saying you were too lenient
in your judgment.

154
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:49,000
So your standing with the public
isn't good,

155
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,400
which could be a problem.

156
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,480
It should be fine.

157
00:08:59,020 --> 00:09:00,810
I'll call my senior at the SPC

158
00:09:00,840 --> 00:09:02,900
in a couple of days and ask about this.

159
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:05,720
Aren't two of your mentors

160
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:08,140
among the most respected figures
in the legal field?

161
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:09,380
Why don't you ask them

162
00:09:10,080 --> 00:09:11,790
to help explain things for you?

163
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:12,840
If they'd been willing to help me,

164
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:13,390
I wouldn't have been

165
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:15,250
assigned here in the first place.

166
00:09:18,670 --> 00:09:19,800
Did you study today?

167
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,700
Go read some more. We'll eat out tonight.

168
00:09:33,940 --> 00:09:38,840
♪ Beneath the Yin Mountains,
across the Chile Plain ♪

169
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:45,950
♪ The sky stretches like a vast tent,
covering the boundless land ♪

170
00:09:46,650 --> 00:09:52,200
♪ The sky stretches wide,
and the plains roll on endlessly ♪

171
00:09:53,410 --> 00:09:58,590
♪ As the wind bends the grass,
cattle and sheep come into view ♪

172
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:05,090
♪ Beneath the Yin Mountains,
across the Chile Plain ♪

173
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:12,340
♪ The sky stretches like a vast tent,
covering the boundless land ♪

174
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:17,590
♪ The sky stretches wide,
and the plains roll on endlessly ♪

175
00:10:19,440 --> 00:10:24,850
♪ As the wind bends the grass,
cattle and sheep come into view ♪

176
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:31,590
♪ Beneath the Yin Mountains,
across the Chile Plain ♪

177
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:38,520
♪ The sky stretches like a vast tent,
covering the boundless land ♪

178
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:44,780
♪ The sky stretches wide,
and the plains roll on endlessly ♪

179
00:11:12,590 --> 00:11:15,340
[Procuratorate Office‌ in Bieshan Prison;
Xijiang Province Bieshan Prison]

180
00:11:20,030 --> 00:11:22,830
How long has it been
since they last saw each other?

181
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:24,610
Almost a lifetime.

182
00:11:42,270 --> 00:11:43,910
The conditions are a bit rough.

183
00:11:43,910 --> 00:11:45,040
Just make do with it.

184
00:11:45,290 --> 00:11:46,320
When we sleep at night,

185
00:11:46,320 --> 00:11:47,650
don't kick me out of bed.

186
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,240
Then you sleep on the inside,

187
00:11:50,240 --> 00:11:51,900
and I'll sleep on the outside.

188
00:11:52,030 --> 00:11:53,150
I wouldn't feel right about that.

189
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:54,440
What if you fall off?

190
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,410
What? Are you going to kick me?

191
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,650
[To: Xia Yingjie] [From: Zhang Lihui]

192
00:12:00,960 --> 00:12:01,600
Lihui.

193
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,440
What is this?

194
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:04,790
Don't, don't...

195
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:05,430
What is this?

196
00:12:05,430 --> 00:12:05,910
What is this?

197
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:07,030
No, no, don't look at it.

198
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:07,670
Let me see.

199
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,670
Let me see.

200
00:12:08,670 --> 00:12:09,000
Okay.

201
00:12:09,230 --> 00:12:10,030
Don't read it.

202
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,250
What's the matter with you?

203
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:15,000
Since graduation,

204
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,960
you've never contacted me

205
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:16,840
or anyone else.

206
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,080
And now this?

207
00:12:22,750 --> 00:12:24,080
It's nothing.

208
00:12:34,480 --> 00:12:35,120
When did you write

209
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:35,960
this letter?

210
00:12:38,270 --> 00:12:39,550
Four years ago,

211
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,450
when you first got to Binjiang.

212
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,600
Then what did you write?

213
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,130
Why didn't you send it to me?

214
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:45,480
I just felt that

215
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,270
whatever I wrote came out wrong,

216
00:12:47,270 --> 00:12:48,440
so I didn't send it.

217
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,090
It's all in the past.

218
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,690
Let's not read it, okay?

219
00:12:53,910 --> 00:12:55,510
It was because of Yu Gaoyuan,

220
00:12:55,750 --> 00:12:56,200
right?

221
00:12:59,270 --> 00:13:00,550
I know you liked him.

222
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:04,550
I'm sorry.

223
00:13:04,550 --> 00:13:05,550
Stop right there.

224
00:13:06,150 --> 00:13:07,630
It wasn't your fault.

225
00:13:08,790 --> 00:13:10,360
And you shouldn't feel guilty

226
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:11,630
just because you liked him—

227
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:13,230
or because I used to like him.

228
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:14,750
And now you're...

229
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:17,200
even punishing yourself like this.

230
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,320
It's not that he wasn't worth it—

231
00:13:19,320 --> 00:13:20,670
it's that no matter who it was,

232
00:13:20,670 --> 00:13:22,000
it wasn't worth making us think

233
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:22,860
or act this way.

234
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:25,810
You don't think

235
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:27,700
I came here because of him, do you?

236
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:30,250
No, I came here because I wanted to.

237
00:13:31,670 --> 00:13:32,510
Here?

238
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:34,840
I feel really calm

239
00:13:35,030 --> 00:13:35,790
here,

240
00:13:36,150 --> 00:13:37,720
and I can see my own growth.

241
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:39,360
Since I was a child,

242
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,640
I've never felt

243
00:13:40,670 --> 00:13:41,450
this relaxed

244
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:42,390
or this free.

245
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:43,750
I feel like I'm

246
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,550
finally at peace with the world.

247
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:47,040
I'm not lying to you.

248
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:51,240
Alright.

249
00:13:55,790 --> 00:13:57,920
-Don't bother reading it.
-Let me see.

250
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,120
Things are

251
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,940
indeed a little dull here.

252
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:12,120
But the work here is anything but simple.

253
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:13,600
There are 4 prison units,

254
00:14:13,850 --> 00:14:14,870
with a total of

255
00:14:15,270 --> 00:14:17,720
1,208 prisoners,

256
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,720
but their combined sentences add up to

257
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,000
more than 20,000 years.

258
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:21,750
Jeez.

259
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:27,670
Here, let me put the cover on.

260
00:14:27,670 --> 00:14:28,670
No, no, don't...

261
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:30,030
Sit, sit.

262
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,600
You're our guest.

263
00:14:32,110 --> 00:14:32,770
Let me do it.

264
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:37,390
Is Lihui adjusting well here?

265
00:14:38,910 --> 00:14:40,240
She's amazing.

266
00:14:41,930 --> 00:14:42,860
She can remember

267
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:44,510
every prisoner's name,

268
00:14:44,790 --> 00:14:45,510
number,

269
00:14:46,030 --> 00:14:46,760
appearance,

270
00:14:46,910 --> 00:14:48,720
conviction, and sentence.

271
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,960
She also has to talk to the prisoners

272
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,560
to understand their appeals

273
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:54,670
and review applications for parole

274
00:14:54,670 --> 00:14:56,120
and sentence reductions.

275
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:56,960
She also has to oversee

276
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,690
inmate discipline and reform.

277
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,270
Even things
like the cleanliness of the bathrooms

278
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:02,930
and the food in the cafeteria—

279
00:15:03,030 --> 00:15:04,670
she keeps an eye on all of them.

280
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:05,440
Tell me,

281
00:15:05,870 --> 00:15:06,930
isn't she amazing?

282
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:18,600
Didn't you go back to visit your mom?

283
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:20,320
I'm not going back.

284
00:15:20,730 --> 00:15:22,000
Every time she sees me, she nitpicks this

285
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,530
and nitpicks that about me.

286
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:24,750
I feel like in her eyes,

287
00:15:24,750 --> 00:15:26,610
I don't have a single good quality

288
00:15:26,750 --> 00:15:29,720
and that I'm nothing but a bunch of tumors
that need to be cut out.

289
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,440
I'm not her family at all.

290
00:15:31,670 --> 00:15:32,910
I'm her patient.

291
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,240
Oh, come on.

292
00:15:36,150 --> 00:15:37,080
Really.

293
00:15:43,790 --> 00:15:44,600
Today

294
00:15:44,870 --> 00:15:45,840
has been the happiest day

295
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,120
I've had in years.

296
00:15:47,890 --> 00:15:49,600
That's definitely because I'm here—

297
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,130
that's why you're so happy.

298
00:15:51,550 --> 00:15:51,960
Yes.

299
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,480
Did you ask Chen Yizhong

300
00:15:58,480 --> 00:16:00,010
to come with you to visit me?

301
00:16:01,030 --> 00:16:02,080
No, I didn't.

302
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,150
He wanted to

303
00:16:04,150 --> 00:16:05,810
come with you on his own, then.

304
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,320
Then why do you think he wanted to?

305
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:09,120
Could it be because he likes you?

306
00:16:09,710 --> 00:16:11,170
He's liked you for so long,

307
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:13,530
and you've never given him any response.

308
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,320
I'm so sleepy.

309
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:23,270
Shouldn't I have brought it up?

310
00:16:24,030 --> 00:16:26,080
It's only a matter of time.

311
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,000
What do you mean, "only a matter of time"?

312
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,240
There's nothing like that between us.

313
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,240
Mark my words—

314
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,600
it's only a matter of time.

315
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,320
Mr. Guo!

316
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:35,360
Mr. Guo! Mr. Guo!

317
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:36,320
Mr. Guo,

318
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,240
hurry, come out!

319
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,000
Something's happened!

320
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:39,060
Prosecutor Zhang!

321
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:40,240
Prosecutor Zhang, hurry and come out!

322
00:16:40,240 --> 00:16:41,020
Something happened!

323
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:41,720
S-Something happened!

324
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:42,920
Hurry up and come out!

325
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:43,600
Mr. Guo!

326
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:46,030
Mr. Guo.

327
00:16:46,550 --> 00:16:47,510
What happened?

328
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:49,270
A prisoner is threatening to harm himself.

329
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:50,200
He insists on talking directly

330
00:16:50,200 --> 00:16:51,080
to Prosecutor Zhang.

331
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,140
No one else will do.

332
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:53,630
Who is it?

333
00:16:53,790 --> 00:16:54,630
Zhou Dazhu, I suppose?

334
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:55,440
About his sentence reduction?

335
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:55,840
Yes,

336
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:56,670
it's him.

337
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,160
You two better hurry.

338
00:16:58,870 --> 00:17:00,470
Let's go. I'll go take a look.

339
00:17:00,670 --> 00:17:02,270
I'll go handle it. You sleep first.

340
00:17:02,270 --> 00:17:02,840
Chen Yizhong,

341
00:17:02,840 --> 00:17:04,369
take good care of her for me!

342
00:17:13,510 --> 00:17:14,270
Do you feel

343
00:17:14,270 --> 00:17:16,200
that she's different from before?

344
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:17,440
Yes.

345
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:20,930
It feels like something...

346
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,859
something about her has changed.

347
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:30,720
Chen Yizhong.

348
00:17:32,790 --> 00:17:34,650
Thank you for coming here with me.

349
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,450
Go inside quickly. It's too cold.

350
00:17:43,640 --> 00:17:44,440
Knock on the wall if you need anything.

351
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,040
I'm staying right next door.

352
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:47,750
Okay.

353
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,350
When we came here,

354
00:18:07,350 --> 00:18:09,110
we actually just wanted to see

355
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,640
how you could endure

356
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,240
working in a place like this.

357
00:18:12,510 --> 00:18:13,770
But after coming here,

358
00:18:14,440 --> 00:18:15,200
I realized

359
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,730
that I was the immature one.

360
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:20,770
You really have changed a lot.

361
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:23,000
Yizhong said the same thing.

362
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,510
He said there's just something different

363
00:18:24,510 --> 00:18:25,350
about you now.

364
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,660
You're exaggerating.

365
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:29,930
To be honest,

366
00:18:30,310 --> 00:18:31,680
when I first got here,

367
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,430
actually...

368
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:35,640
I couldn't sleep for nights on end either.

369
00:18:36,070 --> 00:18:37,550
I just missed Beijing,

370
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,260
missed our school,

371
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:40,860
and missed you.

372
00:18:44,590 --> 00:18:45,480
Then one day,

373
00:18:45,550 --> 00:18:47,010
my mentor brought me here,

374
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,660
and I felt completely healed.

375
00:18:50,110 --> 00:18:50,980
After that,

376
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:52,550
whenever something upset me,

377
00:18:52,550 --> 00:18:54,080
I would come here by myself.

378
00:18:54,440 --> 00:18:55,480
The moment I got there,

379
00:18:55,480 --> 00:18:56,610
I'd feel calm again.

380
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:58,130
It's quite amazing.

381
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:03,600
I think I understand.

382
00:19:04,590 --> 00:19:06,250
But I'm just a little worried.

383
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:07,960
Worried about what?

384
00:19:08,880 --> 00:19:09,720
Worried that you might end up

385
00:19:09,720 --> 00:19:11,590
isolating yourself
more and more like this.

386
00:19:11,590 --> 00:19:12,200
I'm here

387
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:13,400
to become myself,

388
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,960
not to lose myself.

389
00:19:16,070 --> 00:19:18,110
Once I've grown strong enough inside,

390
00:19:18,110 --> 00:19:19,510
I can go back among people

391
00:19:19,580 --> 00:19:20,400
and handle everything

392
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:21,270
calmly.

393
00:19:22,570 --> 00:19:23,720
Don't the strongest plants

394
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:24,850
all grow in

395
00:19:25,400 --> 00:19:26,730
the lonely wilderness?

396
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:27,440
Right?

397
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:38,720
Lihui.

398
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:42,410
I've decided not to resign.

399
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,270
Actually, I knew all along

400
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,730
that you wouldn't resign.

401
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:52,730
That's why I never even
asked you about it.

402
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:54,640
Well,

403
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:56,440
but the law

404
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,790
is made by people.

405
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,240
And it's enforced by people.

406
00:20:00,790 --> 00:20:03,030
So, is the law perfect in every way?

407
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:05,240
And people never make mistakes?

408
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:08,000
Are you trying to comfort me?

409
00:20:08,030 --> 00:20:09,240
Comfort you?

410
00:20:10,510 --> 00:20:11,970
Who's going to comfort me?

411
00:20:13,030 --> 00:20:13,720
I've been here

412
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,000
for over 20 years.

413
00:20:17,350 --> 00:20:20,010
I've received
nearly 100 petitions for appeal.

414
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:22,150
Guess how many of them

415
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:24,810
w-were successfully overturned?

416
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:26,200
How many?

417
00:20:27,640 --> 00:20:28,240
Zero.

418
00:20:32,310 --> 00:20:33,240
Over the years,

419
00:20:33,590 --> 00:20:34,400
I've seen

420
00:20:34,400 --> 00:20:36,440
thousands of prisoners.

421
00:20:37,160 --> 00:20:38,160
Most of them

422
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:40,680
undoubtedly deserved their punishment.

423
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:41,880
But surely, there are

424
00:20:42,550 --> 00:20:44,750
also those who were wrongly convicted.

425
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,550
Sometimes I hate myself too

426
00:20:49,110 --> 00:20:52,040
for not being able to
help them appeal successfully.

427
00:20:52,790 --> 00:20:53,480
Mr. Guo,

428
00:20:54,200 --> 00:20:55,800
please don't think that way.

429
00:20:56,070 --> 00:20:57,350
Hardworking grassroots cadres

430
00:20:57,350 --> 00:20:58,880
like you, who never complain,

431
00:20:58,880 --> 00:20:59,680
are the true backbone

432
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,080
of China's legal system.

433
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:03,240
I'm no backbone.

434
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:04,940
You're better than me.

435
00:21:05,200 --> 00:21:06,920
If you don't want to be a prosecutor,

436
00:21:06,920 --> 00:21:09,000
you can go into business.

437
00:21:10,550 --> 00:21:11,880
What business could I possibly do?

438
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:13,480
I don't know the first thing about it.

439
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:14,510
I just want to...

440
00:21:16,830 --> 00:21:18,400
research legal theory

441
00:21:19,030 --> 00:21:20,750
and make some contribution

442
00:21:21,270 --> 00:21:23,000
to China's legal system

443
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,440
on the theoretical level.

444
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:26,440
I'm really no good at anything else.

445
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:27,450
Yizhong,

446
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,920
if you don't want to
be a prosecutor anymore,

447
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:32,110
you can be a legal scholar.

448
00:21:32,510 --> 00:21:33,070
What?

449
00:21:33,350 --> 00:21:34,280
A legal scholar.

450
00:21:34,510 --> 00:21:35,770
To build the law better

451
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:36,750
from the

452
00:21:36,750 --> 00:21:37,680
source

453
00:21:38,070 --> 00:21:39,310
so that wrongful convictions

454
00:21:39,310 --> 00:21:40,910
can be reduced at their root.

455
00:21:41,310 --> 00:21:42,710
So I could make peace with

456
00:21:42,720 --> 00:21:44,050
what I couldn't change.

457
00:21:45,960 --> 00:21:48,160
That would be worth it, and I'd be happy.

458
00:21:49,350 --> 00:21:50,160
Mr. Guo,

459
00:21:50,160 --> 00:21:52,690
I understand
how much this has weighed on you.

460
00:21:53,680 --> 00:21:54,400
Yizhong,

461
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:55,740
remember this:

462
00:21:56,070 --> 00:21:58,070
as long as you still have the fire in you,

463
00:21:58,070 --> 00:22:00,000
everything else can be worked out.

464
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:02,530
I'll remember that.

465
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,000
I knew

466
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,540
you were someone with ideals.

467
00:22:07,550 --> 00:22:09,200
And y-you look like one too.

468
00:22:18,070 --> 00:22:18,960
Look at Bi.

469
00:22:19,960 --> 00:22:21,760
He has the same seniority as you.

470
00:22:22,270 --> 00:22:23,750
But why hasn't he retired?

471
00:22:26,070 --> 00:22:27,470
Out of sight, out of mind.

472
00:22:28,310 --> 00:22:30,270
How many of your so-called good buddies

473
00:22:30,270 --> 00:22:30,880
ever come by

474
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:31,920
to visit you?

475
00:22:34,790 --> 00:22:35,350
Get out!

476
00:22:44,030 --> 00:22:44,720
Your dad

477
00:22:45,310 --> 00:22:46,350
would rather be a commander without troops

478
00:22:46,350 --> 00:22:47,510
than a commoner.

479
00:22:47,830 --> 00:22:49,160
He's taking it out on me!

480
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:51,810
Change your shoes.

481
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:54,830
Yu, no need to change shoes.

482
00:22:54,830 --> 00:22:55,920
Come on, sit.

483
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:56,270
Dad.

484
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,140
Come on.

485
00:22:57,550 --> 00:22:58,310
Fang,

486
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,210
tone that temper down a bit.

487
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:02,640
It's bad for your health.

488
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,140
Don't listen to her nonsense.

489
00:23:07,030 --> 00:23:08,000
My state of mind

490
00:23:08,200 --> 00:23:09,030
is just fine.

491
00:23:09,580 --> 00:23:11,110
Tomorrow I'll go find Huang and the others

492
00:23:11,110 --> 00:23:12,110
to play gateball.

493
00:23:14,650 --> 00:23:16,310
We brought you some American ginseng.

494
00:23:16,310 --> 00:23:19,570
Steep it in water.
It's good for replenishing your energy.

495
00:23:19,750 --> 00:23:20,640
Yu,

496
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,400
I don't need any supplements.

497
00:23:25,400 --> 00:23:26,720
I want a grandchild.

498
00:23:27,160 --> 00:23:29,090
When will you two finish this task?

499
00:23:29,110 --> 00:23:29,510
Dad,

500
00:23:30,110 --> 00:23:32,110
that's so sudden, out of nowhere.

501
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:35,350
Dad.

502
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:37,760
I'm thinking

503
00:23:37,790 --> 00:23:39,850
we should focus on our careers first.

504
00:23:39,930 --> 00:23:41,350
We'll think about
having children in a couple of years.

505
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:42,810
That's Haohao's idea too.

506
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:43,600
Right?

507
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:58,730
Let's go.

508
00:24:00,350 --> 00:24:02,210
When did you discuss that with me?

509
00:24:02,790 --> 00:24:03,070
What?

510
00:24:03,070 --> 00:24:04,070
When did I discuss what with you?

511
00:24:04,070 --> 00:24:04,680
Didn't we agree

512
00:24:04,680 --> 00:24:06,070
we'd think about having children later?

513
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:07,070
You can see it now.

514
00:24:07,590 --> 00:24:08,270
My dad is getting old,

515
00:24:08,270 --> 00:24:08,880
and his health isn't good.

516
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:10,880
He needs someone to take care of him.

517
00:24:11,110 --> 00:24:12,710
So... w-what are you saying?

518
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:14,270
All the preparations we made before—

519
00:24:14,270 --> 00:24:15,680
we just drop them?
You're just not taking the exam?

520
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:16,480
Why do you only care

521
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:17,550
about yourself?

522
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:18,640
What do you mean, "I only care

523
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:19,720
about myself?"

524
00:24:22,390 --> 00:24:23,000
He's getting old,

525
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:23,830
so now we're supposed to listen to him

526
00:24:23,830 --> 00:24:25,430
and give up everything else?

527
00:24:27,550 --> 00:24:28,610
My father retired,

528
00:24:28,960 --> 00:24:29,480
so now you think

529
00:24:29,480 --> 00:24:31,550
he's of no use to you anymore, is that it?

530
00:24:31,550 --> 00:24:33,000
That I'm no longer a useful stepping stone

531
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:34,110
and having a child with me
would just be a burden, right?

532
00:24:34,110 --> 00:24:35,610
And if, God forbid,
the child were disabled,

533
00:24:35,610 --> 00:24:36,400
then you'd feel even more hard-done-by...

534
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,660
Fang Haohao, what are you talking about?

535
00:24:39,960 --> 00:24:40,590
Did what I just say

536
00:24:40,590 --> 00:24:41,440
mean any of that?

537
00:24:41,440 --> 00:24:42,000
Just now, in there,

538
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:42,940
wasn't that exactly what you meant?

539
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:44,140
I said not right now—

540
00:24:44,170 --> 00:24:45,770
I never said not ever, right?

541
00:24:47,070 --> 00:24:47,730
Yu Gaoyuan.

542
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:50,480
Beijing matters more to you
than this family,

543
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:50,720
doesn't it?

544
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:53,050
Let's not argue anymore. L-Let's go home.

545
00:24:55,330 --> 00:24:55,750
Get on.

546
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:12,380
This one goes on this side.

547
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:14,000
It should be put in like this.

548
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:17,550
Mr. Guo.

549
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:18,680
Mr. Guo.

550
00:25:19,070 --> 00:25:19,680
You're all here.

551
00:25:19,680 --> 00:25:21,270
Just came to say goodbye, Mr. Guo.

552
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:22,720
I told them not to,

553
00:25:22,750 --> 00:25:24,880
but they insisted on coming to see you.

554
00:25:25,070 --> 00:25:26,070
You just didn't want the hassle

555
00:25:26,070 --> 00:25:27,070
of bringing us in.

556
00:25:27,090 --> 00:25:28,400
I just didn't want
the hassle of bringing you in.

557
00:25:28,400 --> 00:25:29,590
Too bad; you had to.

558
00:25:30,110 --> 00:25:31,750
Alright, girl.

559
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:33,200
Well, ever since you two came,

560
00:25:33,200 --> 00:25:34,000
Lihui

561
00:25:34,030 --> 00:25:35,960
has become much more lively.

562
00:25:36,110 --> 00:25:37,040
That's so great.

563
00:25:37,510 --> 00:25:39,640
Seeing her like that makes me so happy.

564
00:25:42,350 --> 00:25:43,480
Have a safe journey.

565
00:25:45,790 --> 00:25:47,520
You're welcome to visit again.

566
00:25:48,920 --> 00:25:50,670
Lihui might not be here then,

567
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:52,280
but I definitely will be.

568
00:25:52,350 --> 00:25:52,920
Okay.

569
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,030
Mr. Guo.

570
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:56,110
Thank you for these past few days.

571
00:25:56,110 --> 00:25:56,550
Why?

572
00:25:56,590 --> 00:25:58,880
The things I've learned here
in these few days

573
00:25:58,880 --> 00:26:00,240
are worth more to me than everything

574
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:02,240
I learned outside in an entire year.

575
00:26:02,790 --> 00:26:03,440
Really?

576
00:26:03,830 --> 00:26:04,310
Yes.

577
00:26:05,250 --> 00:26:06,930
Then w-why does it sound like

578
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:07,850
you're taking a jab at me?

579
00:26:07,850 --> 00:26:08,510
No, I'm not.

580
00:26:08,530 --> 00:26:09,360
No, he wouldn't dare.

581
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:10,920
And he wouldn't do that, Mr. Guo.

582
00:26:10,920 --> 00:26:11,510
His

583
00:26:11,510 --> 00:26:12,440
greatest virtue

584
00:26:12,640 --> 00:26:14,440
is that he's not a smooth talker.

585
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:26,110
Yizhong, do you think

586
00:26:26,480 --> 00:26:27,720
either Du Xiaohui or I

587
00:26:27,720 --> 00:26:28,830
must be the killer?

588
00:26:29,350 --> 00:26:29,880
Go ahead.

589
00:26:30,310 --> 00:26:31,040
Go report me.

590
00:26:31,590 --> 00:26:32,680
What if I run away?

591
00:26:33,350 --> 00:26:34,750
I've got a ticket for 2 PM.

592
00:26:40,400 --> 00:26:41,000
Mr. Guo,

593
00:26:41,920 --> 00:26:42,650
what is this?

594
00:26:44,110 --> 00:26:46,440
Earlier this year, the higher-ups

595
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:48,400
noticed how dull life is here,

596
00:26:48,880 --> 00:26:50,880
so they specially provided a VCR.

597
00:26:51,790 --> 00:26:53,450
The tapes aren't cheap.

598
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:54,680
We can't afford more.

599
00:26:55,590 --> 00:26:56,000
No.

600
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:57,750
I mean, what's playing?

601
00:26:58,350 --> 00:26:59,310
It's a recording of this year's

602
00:26:59,310 --> 00:27:00,480
Spring Festival celebration at the prison.

603
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:01,550
They filmed it.

604
00:27:01,680 --> 00:27:02,310
Well, they just re-copied it

605
00:27:02,310 --> 00:27:03,510
and brought it to me.

606
00:27:05,750 --> 00:27:06,810
What are you doing?

607
00:27:15,510 --> 00:27:16,270
Are all the people in this video

608
00:27:16,270 --> 00:27:17,680
prisoners from here?

609
00:27:19,310 --> 00:27:20,770
W-What's wrong, Yizhong?

610
00:27:27,310 --> 00:27:28,240
Look. Look.

611
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:30,340
Do you know him?

612
00:27:33,810 --> 00:27:34,670
Do you know him?

613
00:27:38,510 --> 00:27:39,570
This looks like...

614
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,000
Xu Zhao.

615
00:27:42,350 --> 00:27:42,920
It's...

616
00:27:52,720 --> 00:27:55,270
I don't think... his name is Xu Zhao.

617
00:27:56,030 --> 00:27:57,030
It's Xu Zhaoyang.

618
00:27:57,590 --> 00:27:58,310
Right, Lihui?

619
00:27:58,310 --> 00:27:59,720
Yes, inmate No. 1093.

620
00:27:59,880 --> 00:28:00,750
Came here the year before last.

621
00:28:00,750 --> 00:28:03,160
Attempted murder—
got a suspended death sentence.

622
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:04,220
Attempted murder?

623
00:28:05,240 --> 00:28:06,510
He tried to kill his wife.

624
00:28:06,510 --> 00:28:07,850
He was having an affair

625
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:09,160
and pushed his wife downstairs.

626
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:11,820
She survived
but was left in a vegetative state.

627
00:28:12,590 --> 00:28:13,310
Then he...

628
00:28:16,830 --> 00:28:18,630
Was the other woman his student?

629
00:28:19,160 --> 00:28:19,640
Yes.

630
00:28:20,830 --> 00:28:21,550
His wife used to be

631
00:28:21,550 --> 00:28:22,510
his student too.

632
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:30,580
Where did he commit the crime?

633
00:28:31,720 --> 00:28:33,400
The Nanchang Intermediate Court
sentenced him.

634
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:35,240
So it should've been in Nanchang.

635
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:36,840
Had he always been in Nanchang?

636
00:28:36,840 --> 00:28:37,830
Did he ever live

637
00:28:37,830 --> 00:28:39,090
anywhere else before?

638
00:28:40,160 --> 00:28:41,720
And did he have any other...

639
00:28:41,750 --> 00:28:42,680
previous names?

640
00:28:42,790 --> 00:28:44,850
He's always been called Xu Zhaoyang?

641
00:28:45,070 --> 00:28:45,480
No.

642
00:28:46,110 --> 00:28:47,000
Um...

643
00:28:47,030 --> 00:28:48,240
when the police and the procuratorate

644
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:49,000
investigated him,

645
00:28:49,000 --> 00:28:50,200
did they ever mention

646
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:51,840
where he lived before

647
00:28:51,920 --> 00:28:53,650
or what kind of work he had done?

648
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,810
Do you know all that?

649
00:28:58,720 --> 00:28:59,270
Yizhong,

650
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:01,920
we should get going. We're running late.

651
00:29:01,920 --> 00:29:03,450
We're really running late.

652
00:29:04,070 --> 00:29:04,400
Mr. Guo...

653
00:29:04,400 --> 00:29:05,680
Mentor, I'll see them off.

654
00:29:05,680 --> 00:29:06,310
Go, go, go.

655
00:29:07,440 --> 00:29:08,510
Let's talk on the way.

656
00:29:08,510 --> 00:29:08,920
Right.

657
00:29:09,030 --> 00:29:10,560
Let's go. Come on. Let's go.

658
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:11,240
Let's go.

659
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:11,920
Let's go. Come on.

660
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:12,880
We'll talk on the way.

661
00:29:12,880 --> 00:29:13,410
Let's go.

662
00:29:18,400 --> 00:29:20,000
Let me know when you arrive.

663
00:29:23,510 --> 00:29:24,200
Yizhong.

664
00:29:24,830 --> 00:29:27,270
Thank you for coming with Yingjie
to visit me.

665
00:29:27,270 --> 00:29:28,440
Don't mention it.

666
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,720
Yingjie is the best girl

667
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:31,680
in the world,

668
00:29:31,750 --> 00:29:32,470
you know?

669
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:37,160
I-I'll get in the car first.

670
00:29:40,110 --> 00:29:40,920
I know.

671
00:29:42,550 --> 00:29:44,150
Make the most of your chance.

672
00:29:45,790 --> 00:29:46,270
And

673
00:29:46,550 --> 00:29:48,070
about Xu Zhaoyang...

674
00:29:48,790 --> 00:29:49,680
That guy...

675
00:29:51,510 --> 00:29:53,110
Maybe I got the wrong person.

676
00:29:53,830 --> 00:29:54,920
I won't overthink it.

677
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:55,880
Zhang told me a long time ago

678
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:57,830
that I'm too obsessed with that matter.

679
00:29:57,830 --> 00:29:59,290
I'll keep looking into it.

680
00:30:01,350 --> 00:30:03,270
If you really are going to look into it,

681
00:30:03,270 --> 00:30:04,800
I think you'll need to check

682
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:06,730
where he lived previously,

683
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,950
as well as his former names,

684
00:30:09,320 --> 00:30:10,960
what he did for a living before,
his blood type,

685
00:30:10,960 --> 00:30:12,960
and all the other relevant details.

686
00:30:14,250 --> 00:30:15,140
I don't think you can ever

687
00:30:15,140 --> 00:30:17,140
just settle into a life as a scholar.

688
00:30:17,160 --> 00:30:18,110
I've said too much.

689
00:30:18,110 --> 00:30:18,640
Let's go.

690
00:30:19,240 --> 00:30:20,270
It'll be dark soon.

691
00:30:20,270 --> 00:30:21,200
Thanks. Thanks.

692
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:21,730
Let's go.

693
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:25,030
What?

694
00:30:25,030 --> 00:30:26,070
Are you shy?

695
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:38,070
Lihui.

696
00:30:39,750 --> 00:30:40,880
I know that being here

697
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:42,270
brings you inner peace

698
00:30:43,110 --> 00:30:43,880
and freedom.

699
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:47,640
But I know you'll come back.

700
00:30:49,030 --> 00:30:50,430
I have a feeling about it.

701
00:30:52,240 --> 00:30:54,110
Then let's leave it to fate.

702
00:31:01,640 --> 00:31:02,160
Go.

703
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:07,020
It's getting late.

704
00:31:07,020 --> 00:31:09,220
I'm worried it won't be safe on the road.

705
00:31:26,400 --> 00:31:27,440
Have a safe trip.

706
00:31:29,310 --> 00:31:30,570
Take care of yourself.

707
00:32:08,350 --> 00:32:10,080
Are you going back to Binjiang?

708
00:32:11,830 --> 00:32:14,310
I want to apply for
Mr. Zhou's graduate program.

709
00:32:14,310 --> 00:32:16,000
Mr. Zhou asked you to come back?

710
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:16,440
No.

711
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:18,520
I wanted to come back myself.

712
00:32:20,830 --> 00:32:21,560
That's good.

713
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:23,640
Eat up.

714
00:32:31,550 --> 00:32:32,150
Yizhong.

715
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:35,110
What happened with that case

716
00:32:35,400 --> 00:32:36,800
you mentioned last time?

717
00:32:38,270 --> 00:32:41,670
Their sentences were changed
to suspended death sentences.

718
00:32:44,240 --> 00:32:46,100
Actually, I've been thinking...

719
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:48,550
maybe that case

720
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:50,360
is also a kind of reprieve

721
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,640
for our relationship

722
00:32:51,880 --> 00:32:53,270
and for your future.

723
00:32:55,160 --> 00:32:56,220
As a prosecutor,

724
00:32:56,440 --> 00:32:57,640
you're already dead.

725
00:32:58,030 --> 00:32:59,630
But as a legal professional,

726
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:01,650
you might be undergoing a rebirth.

727
00:33:03,790 --> 00:33:04,450
Keep going.

728
00:33:19,540 --> 00:33:23,890
[1996, Tianyu Village, Binjiang City]

729
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:11,130
Who's there?

730
00:34:15,510 --> 00:34:17,190
Mom, it's me.

731
00:34:17,550 --> 00:34:18,320
Who?

732
00:34:19,110 --> 00:34:19,920
Sanhua.

733
00:34:20,510 --> 00:34:22,510
I'm your daughter, Yu Sanhua.

734
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:38,730
Your favorite noodles.

735
00:34:38,840 --> 00:34:39,800
Come on, eat up.

736
00:34:41,230 --> 00:34:43,760
H-How did you end up like this?

737
00:34:46,360 --> 00:34:47,510
W-Why didn't you

738
00:34:47,510 --> 00:34:48,770
send any word home?

739
00:34:48,790 --> 00:34:50,389
We all thought you were dead.

740
00:34:52,030 --> 00:34:52,960
Worse than dead—

741
00:34:53,719 --> 00:34:54,850
I wish I had died.

742
00:34:55,880 --> 00:34:57,760
I tried to escape a few times in between,

743
00:34:57,760 --> 00:34:59,670
and whenever they caught me, I got beaten.

744
00:34:59,670 --> 00:35:01,070
They chained me up

745
00:35:01,280 --> 00:35:03,080
and tied me inside the sheep pen.

746
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:04,760
I even wrote you letters.

747
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:07,600
Slow down.

748
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:08,600
Slow down.

749
00:35:10,350 --> 00:35:12,880
It was only after I gave birth to
my third child

750
00:35:13,280 --> 00:35:15,320
that they finally
loosened their grip on me.

751
00:35:15,320 --> 00:35:17,380
Otherwise, I couldn't have escaped.

752
00:35:19,070 --> 00:35:20,030
My daughter,

753
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:22,880
you've had such a hard life.

754
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:27,400
Mom,

755
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:29,900
help me pack some clothes.

756
00:35:30,360 --> 00:35:32,150
And if you have any money, give me some.

757
00:35:32,150 --> 00:35:33,510
I have to leave before dawn.

758
00:35:33,510 --> 00:35:34,280
Why?

759
00:35:35,280 --> 00:35:36,510
I have to run.

760
00:35:37,070 --> 00:35:38,260
What if those two brothers

761
00:35:38,260 --> 00:35:39,510
chase after me?

762
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,590
They paid 7,000 yuan for me.

763
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:51,880
Oh, right.

764
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:53,970
What about Qian Xingliang?

765
00:35:55,630 --> 00:35:57,320
Did he think I ran away?

766
00:35:58,480 --> 00:35:59,440
He didn't come to our house

767
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:01,570
to ask for the bride price back, right?

768
00:36:03,840 --> 00:36:05,170
You gave the money back?

769
00:36:06,110 --> 00:36:07,590
How much did you give him?

770
00:36:09,230 --> 00:36:10,290
Qian Xingliang...

771
00:36:12,110 --> 00:36:14,440
was sentenced to death and sent to prison.

772
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:32,510
Your sister and I both thought

773
00:36:32,510 --> 00:36:33,800
he had killed you.

774
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,110
When he was sentenced,

775
00:36:36,480 --> 00:36:38,920
we asked him for compensation,
but he refused.

776
00:36:38,920 --> 00:36:40,360
So our village sent several men

777
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,880
to smash up his house

778
00:36:42,320 --> 00:36:43,400
and took all the useful things

779
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:44,800
back to our place.

780
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:46,550
In the end, his family

781
00:36:46,550 --> 00:36:48,480
compensated us with 1,300 yuan,

782
00:36:48,800 --> 00:36:49,690
calling it...

783
00:36:50,190 --> 00:36:51,250
funeral expenses.

784
00:37:03,960 --> 00:37:05,550
How can we explain it clearly?

785
00:37:05,550 --> 00:37:07,190
If we explain it clearly, we'll have to

786
00:37:07,190 --> 00:37:08,390
return those things.

787
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:10,930
What are we supposed to give them back?

788
00:37:11,150 --> 00:37:12,800
It's a human life, after all.

789
00:37:13,620 --> 00:37:15,630
No matter how horrible Qian Xingliang was,

790
00:37:15,630 --> 00:37:17,150
we can't let him spend

791
00:37:17,360 --> 00:37:19,710
the rest of his life in prison
because of me.

792
00:37:19,710 --> 00:37:21,330
We weren't the ones who arrested him,

793
00:37:21,330 --> 00:37:22,440
and we didn't sentence him either.

794
00:37:22,440 --> 00:37:24,320
The government said he killed you,

795
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:24,920
right?

796
00:37:26,880 --> 00:37:27,590
Yes...

797
00:37:28,190 --> 00:37:29,990
Then it has nothing to do with us.

798
00:37:30,070 --> 00:37:31,600
It has nothing to do with us.

799
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:52,890
Sir, where are you going?

800
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:53,510
To the county town.

801
00:37:53,510 --> 00:37:55,030
Can you give me a ride?

802
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:56,680
Sure, no problem! Get on!

803
00:38:13,320 --> 00:38:14,850
Put me through to the chief.

804
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:17,560
I have an urgent matter to report to him.

805
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:20,460
Secretary.

806
00:38:20,630 --> 00:38:21,290
Secretary.

807
00:38:26,400 --> 00:38:28,060
Let me brief you on something.

808
00:38:28,480 --> 00:38:29,030
Chief He,

809
00:38:29,510 --> 00:38:30,170
you tell us.

810
00:38:34,480 --> 00:38:35,280
This morning,

811
00:38:35,630 --> 00:38:36,670
the High-Tech Zone Police Station

812
00:38:36,670 --> 00:38:38,530
received a report from a citizen.

813
00:38:38,760 --> 00:38:39,560
It was a woman,

814
00:38:40,420 --> 00:38:41,280
31 years old,

815
00:38:41,770 --> 00:38:43,690
claiming to be Yu Sanhua.

816
00:38:49,760 --> 00:38:50,190
Yes,

817
00:38:50,480 --> 00:38:51,480
the same Yu Sanhua whose body

818
00:38:51,480 --> 00:38:52,480
was dismembered.

819
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:55,170
She said that back then, on her way home

820
00:38:55,180 --> 00:38:56,400
after leaving Qian Xingliang,

821
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:57,920
she was drugged and abducted

822
00:38:57,920 --> 00:38:59,850
by human traffickers at a bus stop,

823
00:38:59,880 --> 00:39:02,140
then sold to a rural area in the mountains

824
00:39:02,320 --> 00:39:03,880
as a wife shared between two brothers.

825
00:39:03,880 --> 00:39:05,740
She had three children with them.

826
00:39:06,070 --> 00:39:07,190
A few days ago, she found an opportunity

827
00:39:07,190 --> 00:39:07,920
and ran back.

828
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:08,840
Currently,

829
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:09,550
we haven't

830
00:39:09,550 --> 00:39:10,760
verified her identity

831
00:39:10,760 --> 00:39:12,110
or her account.

832
00:39:12,760 --> 00:39:14,420
If her identity is confirmed,

833
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:15,880
then her account

834
00:39:15,880 --> 00:39:17,280
won't matter anymore, right?

835
00:39:17,280 --> 00:39:17,880
Exactly.

836
00:39:18,630 --> 00:39:19,670
That would mean

837
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:21,230
Yu Sanhua didn't die,

838
00:39:21,760 --> 00:39:23,760
and Qian Xingliang didn't kill her.

839
00:39:25,630 --> 00:39:26,360
Then when

840
00:39:26,360 --> 00:39:27,400
can we establish her identity?

841
00:39:27,400 --> 00:39:28,150
So far,

842
00:39:28,400 --> 00:39:30,190
what she's said matches

843
00:39:30,840 --> 00:39:31,630
what we already know.

844
00:39:31,630 --> 00:39:32,630
The city authorities

845
00:39:32,630 --> 00:39:33,440
have already asked the police

846
00:39:33,440 --> 00:39:34,300
to protect her.

847
00:39:34,590 --> 00:39:35,440
Test her DNA.

848
00:39:36,190 --> 00:39:37,050
That'll be 100%

849
00:39:37,360 --> 00:39:38,090
conclusive.

850
00:39:38,590 --> 00:39:40,670
Also, reopen the investigation

851
00:39:40,960 --> 00:39:42,510
into that female corpse from back then—

852
00:39:42,510 --> 00:39:43,310
immediately.

853
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:47,880
Why are you drawing my blood?

854
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:48,610
Don't worry.

855
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:50,800
We just want to confirm

856
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:51,930
your true identity.

857
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:54,280
I am Yu Sanhua.

858
00:39:54,880 --> 00:39:55,940
Who else would I be?

859
00:39:56,360 --> 00:39:57,000
I have a few things

860
00:39:57,000 --> 00:39:58,360
I need to verify with you.

861
00:39:58,360 --> 00:39:59,890
Please answer truthfully.

862
00:40:01,800 --> 00:40:02,800
Qian Xingliang

863
00:40:03,550 --> 00:40:04,880
is your husband, right?

864
00:40:05,480 --> 00:40:06,070
Yes.

865
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:12,570
I suppose...

866
00:40:16,840 --> 00:40:17,640
Let me ask you.

867
00:40:18,230 --> 00:40:19,160
Eight years ago,

868
00:40:19,630 --> 00:40:20,670
in 1988,

869
00:40:20,670 --> 00:40:21,480
around August 11th

870
00:40:21,480 --> 00:40:22,480
to 12th,

871
00:40:23,000 --> 00:40:23,800
where were you

872
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:25,770
and what were you doing?

873
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:29,360
If she really is

874
00:40:29,400 --> 00:40:30,360
Yu Sanhua,

875
00:40:31,000 --> 00:40:31,920
what do we do?

876
00:40:35,440 --> 00:40:35,970
Chief He.

877
00:40:40,030 --> 00:40:41,550
If she really is Yu Sanhua,

878
00:40:41,550 --> 00:40:43,110
then it proves that we mishandled

879
00:40:43,110 --> 00:40:44,110
the case back then.

880
00:40:44,110 --> 00:40:45,570
Since we mishandled it...

881
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:47,960
we should admit our mistake, apologize,

882
00:40:47,960 --> 00:40:49,070
provide compensation,

883
00:40:49,070 --> 00:40:51,400
and hold those responsible accountable.

884
00:40:52,190 --> 00:40:53,050
Prosecutor Xu.

885
00:40:53,550 --> 00:40:55,150
Let's follow the proper procedures first

886
00:40:55,150 --> 00:40:57,190
and then retry Qian Xingliang's case

887
00:40:57,190 --> 00:40:58,390
to legally establish

888
00:40:58,550 --> 00:40:59,800
his innocence

889
00:41:00,150 --> 00:41:01,880
and that this was a wrongful conviction.

890
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:02,590
Then...

891
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:05,930
we'll take full responsibility
for our part.

892
00:41:06,070 --> 00:41:07,000
Court Pres. Qiu.

893
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:07,980
Secretary.

894
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:10,360
When this case

895
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:11,710
was handled back then,

896
00:41:11,960 --> 00:41:13,510
Court Pres. Jiang hadn't retired yet,

897
00:41:13,510 --> 00:41:15,510
and I hadn't been transferred here.

898
00:41:16,230 --> 00:41:17,230
But since this case

899
00:41:17,230 --> 00:41:18,880
was adjudicated by our court,

900
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:20,940
we cannot shirk our responsibility.

901
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:22,760
We will deal with
the relevant personnel accordingly.

902
00:41:22,760 --> 00:41:23,490
No leniency.

903
00:41:23,670 --> 00:41:26,330
The murderer was sentenced to
suspended death,

904
00:41:26,710 --> 00:41:28,070
but the victim rode a tractor

905
00:41:28,070 --> 00:41:29,320
and showed up at our door.

906
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:30,630
Isn't that a joke?

907
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:35,630
The police, prosecution, and courts—
all three lines of defense failed,

908
00:41:35,630 --> 00:41:36,230
comrades.

909
00:41:36,550 --> 00:41:37,920
Think about how much damage

910
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:39,110
this does to our credibility,

911
00:41:39,110 --> 00:41:40,510
to the Party's image!

912
00:41:41,190 --> 00:41:42,070
How did the original confession

913
00:41:42,070 --> 00:41:43,150
manage to match the facts

914
00:41:43,150 --> 00:41:44,410
so perfectly?

915
00:41:44,760 --> 00:41:46,360
Our interrogation might...

916
00:41:47,070 --> 00:41:48,670
indeed have been irregular.

917
00:41:53,840 --> 00:41:55,670
Confirm Yu Sanhua's identity immediately.

918
00:41:55,670 --> 00:41:58,270
We absolutely cannot
make a mistake this time.

919
00:41:58,670 --> 00:41:59,070
Also,

920
00:41:59,760 --> 00:42:00,760
which prison is Qian Xingliang

921
00:42:00,760 --> 00:42:01,840
serving his sentence in?

922
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:03,320
Contact the prison immediately

923
00:42:03,320 --> 00:42:05,450
to improve his detention conditions.

924
00:42:08,320 --> 00:42:08,920
Thank you.

925
00:42:16,550 --> 00:42:17,320
No matter who talks to you,

926
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:19,650
push it onto the Adjudication Committee.

927
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:33,760
Did you hear?

928
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:35,480
Hear what?

929
00:42:36,590 --> 00:42:37,400
Yu Sanhua.

930
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:38,880
Yu Sanhua...

931
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:39,670
What about her?

932
00:42:39,670 --> 00:42:41,330
She went home. She's not dead.

933
00:42:43,510 --> 00:42:44,570
Yu Sanhua is not dead...

934
00:42:44,570 --> 00:42:46,770
Let's go outside. Let's go out and talk.

935
00:42:49,730 --> 00:42:52,130
Then the woman
who died wasn't Yu Sanhua...

936
00:42:52,590 --> 00:42:54,150
So who was that body in the river?

937
00:42:54,150 --> 00:42:55,350
Who cares who she was?

938
00:42:55,630 --> 00:42:57,070
The point is, she wasn't Yu Sanhua.

939
00:42:57,070 --> 00:42:58,920
Now we should think about
what we should do.

940
00:42:58,920 --> 00:42:59,920
What should we do?

941
00:43:00,480 --> 00:43:02,070
Exonerate Qian Xingliang immediately!

942
00:43:02,070 --> 00:43:02,960
Keep your voice down.
